DateLabel
@atlaskit/date-label

Props (6)
  appearance     DateLabelAppearance | undefined
  Controls the visual style of the date label. - `neutral` — default grey border style - `warning` — orange border, used for upcoming/near-due dates - `danger` — red border, used for overdue dates
  hasIconBefore  boolean | undefined
  When `true`, an icon is displayed before the label text. The icon shown depends on the `appearance`: - `neutral` → CalendarIcon - `warning` → ClockIcon - `danger` → WarningOutlineIcon
  iconLabel      string | undefined
  The accessible label for the icon. This is passed to the icon's `label` prop and is read by screen readers to convey the icon's meaning. Defaults to a contextual string based on the `appearance`: - `neutral` → `'Calendar'` - `warning` → `'Warning'` - `danger` → `'Danger'` Set to `''` to mark the icon as decorative (when the label text alone is sufficient).
  isSpacious     boolean | undefined
  When `true`, increases the padding and height of the date label for use in more spacious layouts (e.g. forms or detail views). Sets the height to 32px and increases horizontal padding.
  label          string
  The text content to display inside the date label.
  maxWidth       string | number | undefined
  The maximum width of the date label. Accepts a number (treated as px) or a string (e.g. `'50%'`). When the label text exceeds this width it will be truncated with an ellipsis.

